  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Norfloxacin is a fluoroquinolone antibiotic used to treat bacterial infections, including urinary tract infections, gonorrhea, prostatitis, and eye infections such as conjunctivitis. It is an approved medicine, available as an oral antibacterial and also as an ophthalmic preparation, though it is not authorised in the European Union.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q417897&quot;>Wikidata Q417897</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>norfloxacin</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>J01MA06, S01AE02</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB01059&quot;>DB01059</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/4539&quot;>4539</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:100246&quot;>100246</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q417897&quot;>Q417897</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C16H18FN3O3</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>319.336 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
